pySMESH: run the two QR decompositions of System::diagnose on the calling thread.

System::diagnose starts identifyDependentParametersDenseQR (DenseQR) or
identifyDependentParametersSparseQR (SparseQR, the default) with std::async and the default
launch policy, so the runtime may run it on a worker thread while the calling thread computes
the second QR decomposition (FreeCAD's comment above each call). pySMESH runs its algorithms
on the calling thread: a result must not depend on scheduling, and no thread may outlive a
call. With std::launch::deferred the task runs on the calling thread when diagnose waits on
its future, which it does before it reads anything the task writes. The result is the same;
only the thread changes. These two calls are the only thread starts on the solve and diagnose
paths: no PlaneGCS source starts a std::thread or calls std::async elsewhere, and Eigen runs
on one thread (no OpenMP, and System::System calls Eigen::setNbThreads(1)).

